course: dictionary
lesson: 6155
title: Mimic: copying to stay safe, to trick, or to be funny
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To mimic means to copy the way someone or something talks, moves or looks. «The mimic octopus copies the shape and movement of dangerous animals.» It copies their shape, so it can look like something else.
explain: Mimicking can have different reasons. Animals mimic to stay safe or to trick an enemy. People may mimic a teacher's voice to be funny, or to make fun of someone, which can hurt their feelings. Read the words around the word to decide which reason fits.
explain: Use context clues. Ask: who is copying, and why? Then swap in the word copy to test your meaning. If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: To mimic means to copy the way someone talks, moves or looks.
fact: A mimic can also be a noun: a person or animal that is good at copying sounds or actions.
fact: «The mimic octopus, discovered in 1998 off Indonesia, copies the shape and movement of dangerous animals.»
fact: «Male lyrebirds are famous mimics» that copy birdcalls, and even camera shutters, car alarms and chainsaws.
fact: Mimicking someone to make fun of them can hurt, so think about how your copying might make someone feel.
exercise: «The mimic octopus copies the shape and movement of dangerous animals.» What does mimic mean here? | To swim very fast | To sing loudly | *To copy the shape and movement of something else | To hide under a rock forever
exercise: «Male lyrebirds are famous mimics that copy car alarms.» What is a mimic here? | A person who always tells the truth | A kind of camera | *A bird that is good at copying sounds | A tool for cutting wood
exercise: Jada copies her friend's wobbly walk so the class laughs. Why is she mimicking? | To learn a new language | *To be funny, which may make her friend feel hurt | To trick a fish into swimming closer | To stay safe from a hunter
test: «The lyrebird can mimic a chainsaw.» What does mimic mean here? | To be scared of loud noises | To cut down a tree | To buy a chainsaw | *To copy the sound of a chainsaw
test: «Male lyrebirds are famous ___ that copy car alarms.» Which word fits best? | hides | cries | tickles | *mimics
exam: Why does the mimic octopus copy dangerous animals? | To make other octopuses laugh | *To stay safe and trick its enemies | To learn to swim faster | To sleep at the bottom of the sea
